    {
      "id": "2027-Quan-5-2",
      "entry": {
        "title": "2027 Quantitative Methods Mod5-Q2",
        "itemBody": "<p>What is the purpose of dividing data into quantiles?</p>",
        "feedback": {
          "neutral": ""
        },
        "interactionData": {
          "choices": [
            {
              "id": "fb7092ec-78db-4ca3-928f-cc7f95434770",
              "itemBody": "<p>A. To rank the data in ascending order only</p>",
              "position": 1
            },
            {
              "id": "fc8db313-ff03-43eb-8e39-3e66c1358d5c",
              "itemBody": "<p>B. To divide up data into meaningful subsets, allowing for comparison of data based on distinguishing characteristics</p>",
              "position": 2
            },
            {
              "id": "eb2fa899-9357-4b38-b5a2-02f106edd50d",
              "itemBody": "<p>C. To calculate the average value of each data segment</p>",
              "position": 3
            }
          ]
        },
        "scoringData": {
          "value": "fb7092ec-78db-4ca3-928f-cc7f95434770"
        },
        "properties": {
          "shuffleRules": {
            "choices": {
              "toLock": [],
              "shuffled": false
            }
          }
        },
        "scoringAlgorithm": "Equivalence",
        "interactionTypeSlug": "choice"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "2027-Quan-5-3",
      "entry": {
        "title": "2027 Quantitative Methods Mod5-Q3",
        "itemBody": "<p>Why is Bessel’s correction used in sample variance and standard deviation calculations?</p>",
        "feedback": {
          "neutral": ""
        },
        "interactionData": {
          "choices": [
            {
              "id": "0a2256ba-e5b6-4448-96c4-394a9a96eb48",
              "itemBody": "<p>A. To adjust for the underestimation of population variance and standard deviation</p>",
              "position": 1
            },
            {
              "id": "0f92f4ae-5038-4518-ac0e-ddbcb9c226a2",
              "itemBody": "<p>B. To increase the complexity of statistical calculations</p>",
              "position": 2
            },
            {
              "id": "2afc115d-8bd5-4d37-abf3-67d5e7a4354f",
              "itemBody": "<p>C. To align with the total number of observations in the sample</p>",
              "position": 3
            }
          ]
        },
        "scoringData": {
          "value": "0a2256ba-e5b6-4448-96c4-394a9a96eb48"
        },
        "properties": {
          "shuffleRules": {
            "choices": {
              "toLock": [],
              "shuffled": false
            }
          }
        },
        "scoringAlgorithm": "Equivalence",
        "interactionTypeSlug": "choice"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "2027-Quan-5-4",
      "entry": {
        "title": "2027 Quantitative Methods Mod5-Q4",
        "itemBody": "<p>Unlike standard deviation, the mean absolute deviation:</p>",
        "feedback": {
          "neutral": ""
        },
        "interactionData": {
          "choices": [
            {
              "id": "5e7fb1ea-b405-4f07-9837-cfda67c85e26",
              "itemBody": "<p>A. squares each deviation from the mean, providing a measure that is more sensitive to outliers.</p>",
              "position": 1
            },
            {
              "id": "c1826fb3-800a-4b6f-b982-c803bf0d7c77",
              "itemBody": "<p>B. is calculated only for data points above the median, making it suitable for distributions that are asymmetric about the mean.</p>",
              "position": 2
            },
            {
              "id": "fe877bc3-2f84-4c31-ab58-5ae7730d1a76",
              "itemBody": "<p>C. uses the values of the distances from the mean, making it less sensitive to extreme values.</p>",
              "position": 3
            }
          ]
        },
        "scoringData": {
          "value": "5e7fb1ea-b405-4f07-9837-cfda67c85e26"
        },
        "properties": {
          "shuffleRules": {
            "choices": {
              "toLock": [],
              "shuffled": false
            }
          }
        },
        "scoringAlgorithm": "Equivalence",
        "interactionTypeSlug": "choice"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "2027-Quan-5-5",
      "entry": {
        "title": "2027 Quantitative Methods Mod5-Q5",
        "itemBody": "<p>When analyzing a dataset with pronounced skewness and kurtosis, which measure of central tendency is least likely to be affected by extreme values?</p>",
        "feedback": {
          "neutral": ""
        },
        "interactionData": {
          "choices": [
            {
              "id": "fdb0144e-2dec-4be1-8f75-98f57205acf1",
              "itemBody": "<p>A. The mean</p>",
              "position": 1
            },
            {
              "id": "f147e5da-c410-4ff9-8e07-21cc84d947c6",
              "itemBody": "<p>B. The mode</p>",
              "position": 2
            },
            {
              "id": "f0c397f0-e3f3-4c15-afd1-458d351a5900",
              "itemBody": "<p>C. The median</p>",
              "position": 3
            }
          ]
        },
        "scoringData": {
          "value": "fdb0144e-2dec-4be1-8f75-98f57205acf1"
